1 OCCU Maid of Honour of Queen Elizabeth I, Marchioness of Northampton
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Elin Ulfsdotter Snakenborg''', Marchioness of Northampton, also known as Helena, and ''Helena the Red'' for her red hair was born ''Elin Ulfsdotter of Fyllingarum'' in the province of Ostrogothia, Sweden, in eit
2 CONC her 1548 or 1549, and died at the age of 86 on 10 April 1635 at Redlynch, Somerset, the residence of her son Sir Robert Gorges.  She was buried on 14 May 1635 in Salisbury Cathedral. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She came to England as company of princess Cecilia Vasa and became Maid of Honour to Queen Elizabeth I of England, and titular Marchioness of Northampton, by her marriage to William Parr, 1st Marquess of Northampton
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents:  Ulf Henrikssson, lord of Fyllingarum (d.c. 1565), Senator of Sweden, and his wife Agneta Knutsdotter, heiress of Norrnes.
2 CONT
2 CONT Married:
2 CONT # in May 1571 in Elizabeth l's presence in the queen's closet at Whitehall Palace to William Parr, 1st Marquess of Northampton (1513- Oct 1571), son of Sir Thomas Parr and his wife Maud Green, as his third wife. The bride was twen
2 CONC ty-two and the groom fifty-seven. 
2 CONT # secretly about 1576 to Thomas Gorges of Longford.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Elin Snakeborg and Thomas Gorges:
2 CONT # Elizabeth (1578-1659) Elizabeth l stood godmother. m.1 to Hugh Smythe.  m. 2 to Ferdinando Gorges (1565-1647) as his 4th wife.
2 CONT # Francis (b. ca. 1579- d. on or before 1599)
2 CONT # Frances (1580-1649)
2 CONT # Bridget (1584-c. 1634)
2 CONT # Edward (b. 1582/3-d. on or before 1652), first Baron Gorges of Dundalk
2 CONT # Theobold (1583-1647)
2 CONT # Robert (1588-1648)
2 CONT # Thomas (b. 1589-d. after 1624)
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Genealogical Notes==
2 CONT
2 CONT >Contrary to claims presented in some genealogies, Marchioness Helena's ancestry has not been proven to include medieval Viking Earls of Orkney. And also contrary to claims in some genealogies, she seems not to have descended from
2 CONC  the sister of St Bridget of Sweden.
2 CONT
2 CONT >It has been claimed that Helena had no fewer than 92 direct descendants at the time of her death.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Biographical Notes==
2 CONT
2 CONT * from [http://www.kateemersonhistoricals.com/TudorWomenU-V.htm A Who's Who of Tudor Women]
2 CONT
2 CONT >She came to England as a Maid of Honour to Princess Cecilia of Sweden on a state visit in the autumn of 1565, traveling some 400 miles by water and 750 miles on ice and snow in the process, and stayed on when Cecilia left in May 
2 CONC 1566.
2 CONT
2 CONT >She was being courted by William Parr, Marquis of Northampton (August 14,1513-October 28, 1571), who had asked her to marry him, even though he was not legally free to remarry. He promised her a house of her own. At that point, Q
2 CONC ueen Elizabeth stepped in, taking Helena into her keeping at court, possibly as a Maid of Honour. Later she was the First Lady of the Privy Chamber, although without pay. William Parr was the only brother of Queen Catherine Parr, 
2 CONC 6th wife of Henry VIII
2 CONT
2 CONT >Helena and Parr finally married in May 1571, after the death of his first wife, from whom he had been separated for decades. He died soon after, leaving Helena a wealthy widow and, as Marchioness of Northampton, senior to every o
2 CONC ther lady at court save the Queen and the queen's cousin, Margaret Douglas.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1576 she married Sir Thomas Gorges : https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thomas_Gorges
2 CONT
2 CONT >Helena was a patron of the arts, rebuilt Longford House in Wiltshire, (in Tudor times pronounced Langford) - https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Longford_Castle 
2 CONT and was chief mourner at the funeral of Elizabeth Tudor.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==The Gorges Monument==
2 CONT
2 CONT * from http://www.flickr.com/photos/sfoxphotography/4952014672/ 
2 CONT
2 CONT >The Gorges Monument (1635) in Salisbury Cathedral is the tomb of Helena, Marchioness of Northampton and her husband Sir Thomas Gorges. Each side of the elaborate canopy above the tomb displays two cuboctahedra and an icosahedron.
2 CONC  The monument as a whole is crowned by a celestial globe with a dodecahedron on top.
2 CONT
2 CONT * http://salisbury.art.virginia.edu/Student%20Projects
2 CONT
2 CONT >The Gorges monument, c 1635, is located in the north choir aisle in the chapel formerly dedicated to St. Peter and the Apostles.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bibliography:
2 CONT * Two articles, Canon J.M. Fletcher, "The Gorges Monument in Salisbury Cathedral," Wiltshire Archaeological and Natural History Magazine, 46 (1932): 16-34 and K.A. Esdaile, "The Gorges Monument in Salisbury Cathedral," Wiltshire A
2 CONC rchaeological and Natural History Magazine, 50 (1942-44): 53-62.
2 CONT
2 CONT * See also Roy Spring, Salisbury Cathedral, The New Bell's Cathedral Guides, London, 1987, 128-130.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Weblinks==
2 CONT
2 CONT * http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/Bios/HelenSnakenborg.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Biography==
2 CONT
2 CONT * [http://www.worldcat.org/oclc/9346668 Bradford, Charles A. Helena, Marchioness of Northampton. London: G. Allen & Unwin ltd, 1936. Print.]
2 CONT * [http://hdl.handle.net/2027/wu.89035454594 Sjögren, Gunnar. Helena Snakenborg: En Svenska Vid Elisabet I:s Hov. Stockholm: Askild & Kärnekull, 1973.]
2 CONT
2 CONT ==References==
2 CONT
2 CONT * Sjöström (2007): "Scandinavian medieval descendants of Charlemagne: A detailed genealogy of the issue of Agnes Haakonsdottir, of the so-called Fairhair dynasty", Foundations - Journal of the Foundation for Medieval Genealogy 2: 
2 CONC 4 (2007, July), ISSN 1479-5078, pp 253–276
2 CONT * EARL OF ESSEX WILLIAM6 PARR (SIR THOMAS OF KENDAL5, WILLIAM4, THOMAS3, JOHN2, WILLIAM MARQUESS OF1) was born August 14, 1513 in Kendall, Westmoreland, England, and died October 28, 1571 in Warwick, Warwickshire, England. He marr
2 CONC ied (1) HELENA HENRICKSSON SNAKENBORG. He married (2) ELIZABETH BROOKE 1547, daughter of GEORGE BROOKE and ANNE BRAYE. She was born June 12, 1526 in Cobham, Kent, England, and died April 02, 1565 in Blackfriars Church, London, Cou
2 CONC nty Greater London, England. He married (3) BARONESS ANNE BOURCHIER 1551 in Prescot, Lancashire, United Kingdom, daughter of WILLIAM BOURCHIER and MARY SAY. She was born 1512, and died 1571.
2 CONT * https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Helena,_Marchioness_of_Northampton
2 CONT * http://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00247787&tree=LEO
2 CONT * https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/B%C3%A5%C3%A5t_nr_3#TAB_11
2 CONT * Helena ulfsdotter bååt, dotter till ulf henriksson bååt, kom till england med prinsessan cecilia vasa ca 1564, och blev kvar i england, gifte sig först med drottning catherine Parrs bror William 1571 , men william dog ett par må
2 CONC nader efter bröllopet, och då blev Helena en rik änka, enligt wikipedia. hon var känd som markisinnan av Northampton, för william var markis av Northampton. var ingift i den engelska kungafamiljen tack vare att william parr var dr
2 CONC ottning catherines bror. senare gifte hon om sig med Thomas gorges, utan drottning elisabeths tillstånd som ansåg att hon gifte ner sig.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://historyofparliament.com/2024/03/14/helena-marchioness-of-northampton/
