1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Hogenskild Nilsson Bielke==
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hogenskild_Bielke '''Hogenskild Bielke'''] (1538 - 3 June 1605), was a Swedish baron, court official and riksråd. He was one of the more prominent leaders of the Swedish nobility in their power strug
2 CONC gle against royal authority during the 16th-century.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Life===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''He was the son''' of riksråd Nils Pedersson of Åkerö and [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anna_Hogenskild Anna Hogenskild of Hedensö]. In 1569 married Anna Sture (1541-1595), daughter of [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Svante_Sten
2 CONC sson_Sture Svante Stensson Sture] and [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Martha_Leijonhufvud Martha Leijonhufvud] and thus niece of queen [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Margaret_Leijonhufvud Margaret Leijonhufvud].
2 CONT
2 CONT '''He was raised at court''', his mother being a lady-in-waiting, and became the playmate of prince [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Magnus,_Duke_of_%C3%96sterg%C3%B6tland Magnus, Duke of Östergötland] and courtier of king [https://
2 CONC en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gustav_I_of_Sweden Gustav I of Sweden] in 1556. He was made member of the royal council by [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eric_XIV_of_Sweden Eric XIV of Sweden] and served as a military commander in the [http
2 CONC s://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Northern_Seven_Years%27_War Northern Seven Years' War].
2 CONT
2 CONT '''In the autumn of 1573''', a plot was prepared to assassinate John III. The plot was led by [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charles_de_Mornay Charles de Mornay], who was in contact with [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Christina_of
2 CONC _Denmark Christina of Denmark] and the French ambassador in Copenhagen [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charles_Dan%C3%A7ay Charles Dançay]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''John III was to be''' killed during a swords dance performed by Scottish mercenaries at the party which was to be given in October that year before the Scottish mercenaries departure to the Baltic, and the king's brother [https
2 CONC ://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charles_IX_of_Sweden Duke Charles] was to be placed upon the throne. The plot did not materialize as de Mornay lost his nerve and never gave the sign to the mercenaries to take action. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''In September 1574''', the plot was revealed and Charles de Mornay was arrested, interrogated and executed. It was never made clear who participated in the plot, but it was noted that the suspected conspirators Hogenskild Bielke
2 CONC , [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gustaf_Ban%C3%A9r Gustaf Banér] and [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pontus_De_la_Gardie Pontus De la Gardie] often gathered at meetings in the apartment of Princess [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pr
2 CONC incess_Elizabeth_of_Sweden Elizabeth of Sweden] with Princess [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Princess_Cecilia_of_Sweden Cecilia of Sweden], and Charles de Mornay claimed that one of the things which were agreed upon by the conspir
2 CONC ators was to raise the dowry of Elizabeth from 100,000 to 150,000, so to make it possible for her to make a marriage of higher status, which would refer to the suggested marriage between Elizabeth and [https://en.wikipedia.org/wik
2 CONC i/Henry_III_of_France Henry III of France], in which the French ambassador had expressed himself impressed by everything regarding Elizabeth with the exception of her dowry. The two royal sisters and their brother Charles were som
2 CONC ewhat compromised, though neither they, Bielke, Banér or De la Gardie was openly accused of their suspected involvement.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''When the king and''' queen visited their son [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sigismund_III_Vasa Sigismund III Wasa] in Reval in 1589, he and Axel Bielke was appointed to serve as regent during their absence. He was described as 
2 CONC clever and skillful and worked to increase the power of nobility against the crown. He sided with Sigimund III against Duke Charles. His son Svante fled to Denmark after the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/War_against_Sigismund War
2 CONC  against Sigismund] to avoid execution. Hogenskild was tried during the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Link%C3%B6ping_Bloodbath Linköping Bloodbath] in 1600, but was imprisoned rather than executed. In 1605, however, he was found 
2 CONC to have been involved in a correspondence judged as treasonable alongside his daughter [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ebba_Bielke Ebba Bielke]. He was executed for treason in Stockholm.
2 CONT
2 CONT /////
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Bielke_af_%C3%85ker%C3%B6_nr_8#TAB_25 '''Hogenskild Bielke''', friherre '''till Läckö'''], herre till Stora Dala i Dala socken, Skaraborgs län, Åkerö i Bettna socken, och Nynäs i Bälinge socke
2 CONC n, båda i Södermanlands län, samt Ulfåsa i Ekebyborna socken, Östergötlands län. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Född 1538 på''' Stora Dala. Studerade vid Åbo latinskola 1547-1551, vid universitetet i Wittenberg 1551 samt vid Odense latinskola 1554-1555. Hovsven hos hertig Magnus 1556, hos Gustaf I 1557 och hos hertig Erik 1558. Köksmästa
2 CONC re hos hertig Erik 1559. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Riddare 1561. Riksråd''' 1562. Sändebud till koadjutorn i Riga, hertig Christoffer av Mecklenburg 1563. Förrättade räfsteting i Finland och Västerbotten enligt brev 1564. Deltog i danska kriget 1565. Kommendant på Varbergs slot
2 CONC t 1566. Fältöverste i Småland samt Öster- och Västergötland 1567. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Tillfångatagen av''' danskarna 1568-01-00, utväxlad 1568-12-18. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Friherre 1569-07-10''' vid konung Johan III:s kröning och fick Läckö till friherrskap 1571. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Rådsherre hos hertig''' Carl 1569. Slottslofven i Stockholm 1570. Ledde stora skeppsflottans utrustning 1570. Sändebud vid utväxlingen av fredstraktaterna med Danmark i Knäred 1570, vid gränsmöte med danskarna i Avaskär 1572 ti
2 CONC ll Polen 1572. Medlem av domstolen över Carl de Mornay 1574. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Erhöll Memmings''' och Bobergs härad i Östergötland i förläning 1576. Ståthållare över Östergötland 1576. Lagman över Uppland och Norrland 1577. Sändebud vid gränsmöte med danskarna i Sjöryd 1580. Erhöll Jaggowals gårdslän i Es
2 CONC tland i förläning 1581 ståthållare över Stockholm, Uppland, Västmanland och Norrland 1589. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Såsom anhängare''' av konung Sigismund insatt i fängelse på Vadstena 1599. Anklagad inför ständerna i Linköping 1600. Vistades i fängelse på Gripsholm 1600-1605. Anklagad inför ständerna i Stockholm 1605 och dömd till döden 160
2 CONC 5-05-04 samt avrättad 1605-06-03 på Stortorget i Stockholm. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Begraven i Gråmunkeklostret''' (Riddarholmskyrkan) vid västra dörren, men fördes sedan till Ekebyborna kyrka, där han jämte sin fru ligger i en präktig grav. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Gift 1569-06-21''' Hörningsholm med sin farbroders svägerska grevinnan '''Anna Sture''', född 1541-01-29 på Stegeborg, död 1595-03-09 i Stockholm, dotter av riksrådet Svante Stensson Sture, greve till Stegeholm och Västervik ([
2 CONC https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Natt_och_Dag_nr_13 Natt och Dag]) och Märta Eriksdotter ([https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Leijonhufvud_nr_26 Leijonhufvud]).
2 CONT
2 CONT * http://www.nad.riksarkivet.se/sbl/Presentation.aspx?id=18165
2 CONT * http://wadbring.com/historia/sidor/lacko.htm#hogen
2 CONT <br/>
2 CONT <br/>
