1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Kristina Karlsdotter Bonde==
2 CONT
2 CONT (TAB 1)
2 CONT
2 CONT Erik Eriksson the elder, (son of Erik Nielssen Gyllenstjerne ), to Demstrup in Jutland, Kråkerum in Mönsterås parish and Fågelvik in Tryserum parish (both in Kalm.) And St. Bjurum in Bjurum parish Skaraborg County. Arrived in Swed
2 CONC en and received 1446 take over his brother-in-law pantland Öland with Borgholm Castle. Be a knight 381449-02-25 and the Council of State 1450-05-13. King Karl Knutsson's chiefmaster 1450. Envoy to the meeting with the Danish in Ha
2 CONC lmstad, Sweden. Sender to King Kristian I in Denmark 1453-05-07. Lagman in Ten Years Lagsaga s. Å. Was at the handover of Borgholms Castle to the Danes 1456-10-10 abducted in Danish captivity and lost at Kristian I's throne settle
2 CONC ment in Sweden 1457 team members and Kråkerum's estate. Envoy to the meeting with the Danes in Halmstad 1468-07-29 and in Lübeck 1469-10-20. Retained the 1468 team team. Envoy to the resignation treaty between the Swedish National
2 CONC  Council and King Kristian 1471-09-08 and to the peace treaty with the Danes in Kalmar 1472-07-02, 1473-08-17 and 1474-08-19. During his last years, Stäkeholm County (Tjust, Kinds and Outer Heroes) had been in forgiveness to her d
2 CONC eath. Died 1477. He exchanges the star in the weapon color from silver to gold [RHKn]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married 1446-09-29 at Svartsjö Castle with Kristina Karlsdotter , born 1432 (?) And who lived widow yet 1492, but her succession was held from 1500-01-25, daughter of King Karl VIII Knutsson ( Bonde ) and his 1st Meal Birgitta T
2 CONC uresdotter ( Bielke ).
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Children:==
2 CONT
2 CONT * Carin died as young.
2 CONT * Margareta's death as young.
2 CONT * Lisbet died as young.
2 CONT * Abraham Eriksson . Man in Kalmar. Death 1514. See Tab. 2nd
2 CONT * Nils Eriksson . Knight and counselor. Death 1495. See Tab. 3
2 CONT * Erik Eriksson the younger one . Knight and counselor. Death 1502. See Tab. 4th
2 CONT * Brigitta , dead young.
2 CONT * Knut Eriksson . Cited only in the grandfather's wife. Karl Knutsson's testament 1470, when he receives 'a red fleece coat, lined with hermelin and red flute to a shirt and a band of Kastidorian stena'.
2 CONT * Kerstin Eriksdotter , lived widow on St. Bjurum 1 yet 1500-01-25. Married 1473-01-23 with the knight, the council and the teamman at Närke Hans Åkesson (Tott), to Bjurum and Frötuna, died 1492-12-20 at the farm in Frölunda socke
2 CONC n Älvsborg County, killed by a farmer. 2
2 CONT * Görvel Eriksdotter , died around 1495. Married 1488 with the statue holder at Akershus, Knight Alfsson ( Three Roses ) , Knight Alfsson, in his 1st married [married 2: o with Metta Ivarsdotter, who lived in Denmark still 1525 in
2 CONC  her 2: married married (married 1: o with the Norwegian council Anders von Bergen, died in 1491. married 3: o 1504-11-17 with the governor, the knight and the council Svante Nilsson (Sture), in his 2nd marriage, death 1512) daugh
2 CONC ter by Ivar Jenssen (Animal), who in the gun brought two horns, and Christina Pedersdotter Oxe to Assarbo], murdered during the shelter 1502-08-18 at Akershus. 3
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Gyllenstierna_af_Lundholm_nr_3 Gyllenstierna of Lundholm No. 3 Geneology]
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Parents==
2 CONT
2 CONT Karl Knutsson, King Karl VIII Knutson (Son of Knut Bonde, Tab. 6 ), probably born 1408, died 1470-05-15. King of Sweden 1448-06-20. Elected to King in Norway 1449. Lost his Norwegian Crown in 1450. Abandoned as King in Sweden in 1
2 CONC 457, was recalled to King in the fall of 1464. Refused the Crown 1465. Again called King 1467-09. 
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married 1: o 1429-02-28 on Ekholmen with Birgitta Turesdotter (Bielke) , daughter of the knight and Ture Stensson ( Bielke ) and Birgitta Abrahamsdotter (bullhead). 
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married 2: o 1438-10-05 in Stockholm with Katarina Karlsdotter (head of the head) , daughter of the Swedish council Karl Ormsson ( head of the head ) and Märta Gregersdotter ( Aspenäsätten)
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married 3: o 1470 with her fiancé Kristina Abrahamsdotter , possibly daughter of the hardener in Raseborg's western hemd Abraham Pedersson (half-animal).
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Children: In married 1: o with Birgitta Turesdotter (Bielke):==
2 CONT
2 CONT * Tours Karlsson, died young before 1447-06-23.
2 CONT * Kristina Karlsdotter, lived 1492-06-11. Married 1446-09-27 at Svartsjö with the knight and the council, King Charles's headmaster and the team in Tiohärad Erik Eriksson ( Gyllenstierna ).
2 CONT
2 CONT http://finnholbek.dk/getperson.php?personID=I12689&tree=2
