1 NAME Nils /Johansson Bröms/
2 GIVN Nils
2 SURN Johansson Bröms
2 _MARNM Johansson Bröms
2 NICK NILS Jönsson Bröms
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1510
2 PLAC Kvillinge 
2 ADDR
3 STAE Östergötlands län
3 CTRY Sweden
1 DEAT
2 DATE BEF 1580
2 ADDR
3 CITY Normlösa
3 STAE Östergötland County
3 CTRY Sweden
1 OCCU Amiral
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Nils Johansson, Bröms Ruska=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Johan Nilsson Ruska, til Ryssby and Anna Jönsdotter Bröms 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT *Married: in 1558 to '''Karin Larsdotter (Hjortösläkten)''' (EÄ), lived at Lidhem, Locknevi (Smål), daughter of the castle lord at Stegeborg in 1555 Lars Tidemansson (to Forsa, now Sturefors (Östg), died in 1562 and Ingeborg Bengt
2 CONC sdotter ( Slatte ), who held Hjortö, Hjorted sn (Smål) in 1525. (She was married 2nd Christiern Johansson ( Lilja av Värnäs ))
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[http://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Br%C3%B6ms_nr_161#TAB_4 Adelsvapen Geneology]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Nils Jonsson Bröms (son of Johan Nilsson Ruska Tab. 3 ), Ship's Chief of Staff at the fleet, castle lord at Nyköping 1568, admiral of the small fleet 1569 (EÄ), lived in 1575 in March, when he received Johan III's command to direc
2 CONC t the copperworks in Dalhem (Smål) and at Åtvid (Östg) (EÄ band 9 p. 262). Took mother's name. Already in 1533 he bought a farm in Flenshult, Karlstorps skate, Aspeland county, when three sisters Anna, Kerstin and Margareta Hansdö
2 CONC tter sold to their uncle's son, whose wife Karin Larsdotter (Hjortösläkten) owned the farm in 1579 (1) . The three sisters also sold in 1533 Dönnemåla and Gissemåla and Kvavhult in Vimmerby sn (2) . They were daughters of Elin Nil
2 CONC sdotter and Hans Jeppesson of Flenshult, Elin daughter of Karin Offesdotter (Bååt) who was married 1st to Nils Jonsson Ruska ennobled in 1486, Nils Jonsson Bröm's grandfather. Flenshult and other farms were therefore bought by Nil
2 CONC s Jonsson's cousins, granddaughters of his grandfather Nils Jonsson Ruska (3) . Married in 1558 to Karin Larsdotter (Hjortösläkten) (EÄ), lived at Lidhem, Locknevi (Smål), daughter of the castle lord at Stegeborg in 1555 Lars Tide
2 CONC mansson (to Forsa, now Sturefors (Östg), died in 1562 and Ingeborg Bengtsdotter ( Slatte ), who held Hjortö, Hjorted sn (Smål) in 1525. (She was married 2nd Christiern Johansson ( Lilja av Värnäs ))
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Child Sequence Uncertain=
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Nils'''. District Chief. son of Nils Jonsson Bröms Tab. 4 ) Häradshövding in Tunalän (Smål) 1581, Johan III.'s court servant 1582. Lived 1611 17/8 but was dead 1612 16/1 (settlement of inheritance). To Lidhem, Locknevi (Smål)
2 CONC . Inherited from stepfather Christiern Johansson in 1586 (9) . Nils Nilsson Bröms had a Persian concubine (=frilla) and many illegitimate children, according to Archbishop Abraham Angermannus in Locknevi in ​​1596 when he was to s
2 CONC end a letter that he promised to renounce with immediate effect his "abominable bolery and sodomist life, because bolares would not inherit God's kingdom but is thrown into the lake that burns with fire and brimstone.” Nils refuse
2 CONC d to sign but thought, with God's help, to look around after marriage soon (10). Married to Margareta Andersdotter Rosenstråle . Lived at Locknevi left by her husband in the parish of the same name, lived in 1622 (EÄ band 9 p. 262
2 CONC ). (Married 2nd Per Svensson Bagge av Söderby , died before 1625.) The statement in EÄ that Nils Nilsson died childless is incorrect. The wife Margareta Rosenstråle appears after his death with Nils' brother Arvid Nilsson Bröms an
2 CONC d brother-in-law Knut Eriksson to Kvavhult (married to Margareta Nilsdotter Bröms) in an estate dispute as representative of his fatherless children in 1616 (11) . Further evidence appears in the will dated Kvavhult, Vimmerby lfs 
2 CONC 1657 12/6 by Knut Eriksson's daughter Cecilia Knutsdotter Sabel (Göta court of appeals) when she mentions that she and her sisters were disinherited by maternal uncle Arvid Nilsson Bröms, who thus left an inheritance to siblings a
2 CONC nd not to own children.
2 CONT * '''Arvid'''. Knekhtövidsman. son of Nils Jonsson Bröms Tab. 4 ) introduced in 1627 no. 161 Knekthövitsman (EÄ) to Lidhem. Born in the 1560s (own information; over 60 years 1627; EÄ band 9 p. 262). Was dead in 1644 7/3 according 
2 CONC to the exchange lot referred to as having happened "by passport 13 years ago", mentioned in Cecilia Sabel's will in 1657; see above). Married 1st Märta Pedersdotter Siöblad to Lida. Married 2nd 1629 28/10 at Lidhem (EÄ) to Karin A
2 CONC rvidsdotter Drake af Hagelsrum in her 2nd marriage. ( married 1st before 1623 to deceased lieutenant Anders Biörnsson (7) ) According to priest Locknevi, she donated to Locknevi church in 1636 after her beloved husband (8). Karin 
2 CONC Drake was gifted this morning 1629 Slättfall, Vimmerby lfs and Ugglefall, Vena sn (Smål) (Drakeska arkivet, UUB). Childless
2 CONT * '''Anna Nilsdotter Bröms.''' Wife Anna to Hasselby, Lofta sn (Smål) 1597, to Dentersta, Vadsbro sn (Söd) 1610. Died about 1639 in Djuvanäs, Björkö sn, Östra Härad (Kronoberg County). Married to Nils Hansson (Björnram) ennobled (
2 CONC to Hasselby, Lofta sn (Smål), lieutenant under Sven Månsson's banner in 1589 (4) . May well-born Lars Björnram see the noble family Björnram af Helgås no. 204 . lived 1657, married to daughter Kerstin Nilsdotter, and mentioned in 
2 CONC Cecilia Knutsdotter Sabel's will dated Kvavhult 1657 12/5 as one of those who dispossessed her and two sisters from inheritance after uncle Arvid Bröms (See under Margareta Nilsdotter Bröms )
2 CONT * '''Margareta Nilsdotter Bröms''' Lived in the 1640s at Kvavhult, Vimmerby lfs (5) . “Married to an unsaved man; spent under him their goods” (6) . Married to Knut Eriksson (sable under 2 stars) (to Hämeekylä, Bjärnå sn where the
2 CONC  arms are) Underståtholder at Nöteborg. see noble family Sabelstierna no. 206 .
2 CONT
