1 NAME Johan /Kinnemond/
2 GIVN Johan
2 _MARNM Kinnemond
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1590
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1638
1 OCCU
1 TITL Colonel
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *[https://et.wikipedia.org/wiki/Johan_Kinnemond Wikipedia (Estonian)]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Johan Kinnemond''' ('''John Kinninmonth'''; died in 1638) was a Scottish officer in Swedish service. Colonel of Närke-Värmland regiment, commander of Pillau fortress in Prussia and later of Nöteborg castle in Russia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Owner of the Enneberg estate in Livland.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a relative of colonels Patrick and Thomas Kinnemond, as Thomas inherited his Enneberg estate. Johan Kinnemond's widow Christina Ulfsparre wanted that an unnamed nephew (sister's son) of his late husband would inherit instea
2 CONC d. According to the document the nephew had served under uncle's command in Nöteborg. This plan did not come to fruition, probably because the Norrköping law did not allow for female-line inheritance.
2 CONT
2 CONT The only Scottish officer that could match the description is [https://www.geni.com/people/David-Duddingston/6000000216191300833?through=6000000216191309821 David Dudinstein] (David Duddingston):
2 CONT *he served in Nöteborg in 1634
2 CONT *he married [https://www.geni.com/people/Cecilia-Ivarsdotter-Ulfsparre/6000000216191309821 Cecilia Ulfsparre], the sister of Christina Ulfsparre
2 CONT *he was probably the son of Stephen Duddingston of Sandford and Eupham Kinninmonth.
2 CONT
2 CONT If that is true, then John Kinnemond was the son of [https://www.geni.com/people/Patrick-Kinninmonth-of-that-Ilk/6000000018848170454?through=6000000013526712309 Patrick Kinninmonth of Craighall] and Christian Beaton. Patrick and T
2 CONC homas Kinnemond were probably his nephews too, but because they descended from his brother, they were eligible for inheritance under the 1604 Norrköping inheritance law.
1 FAMS @F6000000207953607829@
1 RFN geni:6000000207953607823
