1 OCCU Lagman i Uppland, Väpnare1440, riddare1442, riksråd1457, lagman i Uppland 1487
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * https://sok.riksarkivet.se/sbl/Presentation.aspx?id=10299
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Mats Ödgislason (Lillie af Greger Mattssons ätt), till Lagnö and Ingeborg Gregersdotter (Aspenäs)
2 CONT
2 CONT * Grav i Riddarholmskyrkan: https://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Riddarholmskyrkan#Forbuska_graven_eller_De_la_Gardieska_graven
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Lillie_af_Greger_Mattssons_%C3%A4tt_nr_6 Adelsvapen Geneologies Lillie of Greger Mattsson's family no. 6]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''TABLE 2'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Greger Mattsson (son of Matts Ödgislesson, Tab. 1), to Tyresö in the same parish, Stockholm county, which he inherited from his grandmother. Was a squire in 1440, knight 1443-06-15 and councilor in 1457. Was King Karl's chieftain 
2 CONC Raseborg As a brother-in-law to Erik Axelsson, he probably assisted in the overthrow of the state in 1457, at least he participated in the decisions that were implemented in the council shortly afterwards, but then King Kristian i
2 CONC n 1463 demanded the opinion of the councilors about Jöns Bengtsson, he participated in all three decisions, which went out on his imprisonment. Sent together with others in 1464 to Danzig to summon King Charles again. Was present 
2 CONC when Jöns Bengtsson was forced to give up his worldly power in the fall of 1466 and was sent s. å. to Raseborg to persuade King Karl to return. After his death in 1470, he stood by Sten Sture's side. Lagman in Västmanland 1478–148
2 CONC 6. Received Stegeborg castle and county 1487-09-03. Lagman in Uppland 1487 until his death. Lived 1494-02-00 21 , but was dead s. å. 22 , when succession was carried out after him 5/11 (according to the tombstone death 1493-03-23)
2 CONC  18 . '''Married 1st to Anna Johansdotter , died approx. 1453, daughter of the knight and councilor Johan Nilsson Gädda and Elin Axelsdotter Brahe .''' Married 2nd shortly after 12/06/1455 to Ramborg Gustafsdotter , died 13/11/149
2 CONC 2. Daughter of the knight and councilor Gustaf Ulfsson Sparre of Hjulsta and Ängsö and Kristina Folkadotter Rossviksätten who carried a Boat in the coat of arms.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1. '''Brita Gregersdotter ,''' died before 1504-03-12 but after 1503-11-01 when she made a will. Buried in Krokek's monastery/E. Married 1468-10-24 (morning gift) to the knight, councilor and lawman in Södermanland Åke Jönsson (
2 CONC  Svarte Skåning ), to Åkerö, in his 2nd marriage (married 1st 1445-01-18 to Mechtild Clausdotter (Plata), who was still alive in 1460), died in 1494.
2 CONT * 1. '''Marina Gregersdotter ,''' was dead in 1459, when she was inherited by her father.
2 CONT * 2. '''Matthias Gregersson .''' Student in Greifswald 1487. Master there. 1490, then doctor decretorum. Enrolled at the University of Cologne 1492-09-07. Kanik in Uppsala. Provost in Strängnäs 1494-11-16. Bishop of Strängnäs 1501
2 CONC -08-27. Riksråd 1502. Was on the side of the Sturars. Bequeathed to Denmark in 1504. Participated in the meetings in Malmö and Copenhagen in 1512 and 1513. Passed after Sten Sture's death in 1520 to King Kristian, but was beheaded
2 CONC . Oh. 8/11 in Stockholm's bloodbath, regardless he and the other councilors agreed to Kristian's acceptance as king, and persuaded the common people to celebrate him and helped at his coronation. (SBL:23 p64 + p67; PhT 1951 p101; 
2 CONC StrHm:1 p373, 455ff; OxoVasa p92f)
2 CONT * 2. '''Bengt Gregersson .''' Knight and Councillor. Died before 1501. to Tyresö and Lagnö. Squire. Riksråd as early as 1485. Knighted in 1497. Held the county of Frösåker as a fief. Lived in 1499. but was dead on 1501-03-12. Marr
2 CONC ied to Märta Arentsdotter , after which inheritance was executed in 1514, daughter of the knight and councilor Arent Bengtsson ( looking back wolf ), to Nynäs, and his 2nd wife Hebbla Albrektsdotter Bydelsbach .
2 CONT * 2. '''Folke Gregersson .''' Knight and Councillor. Died 1507. to Åkerö in Bettna parish, Södermanland county. Was knighted on 16-12-1497, when he received Viste county as a fief. Councilor 1504. Died 1507-04-19. He was accused i
2 CONC n 1497 by vicar Otto in Fröslunda for raping him and eating meat on Fridays. Married 1499-09-15 in Söderköping (morning gift) to Brita Hansdotter , died after 1539-01-16 and before 1541-03-12. Daughter of the knight and lawman in 
2 CONC Närke Hans Åkesson Tott till Bjurum and Frötuna and Kerstin Eriksdotter Gyllenstierna af Lundholm .
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Omnämns i följande [http://www.dokpro.uio.no/perl/middelalder/diplom_vise_tekst_2016.prl?b=13799&s=n&str= Diplomatarium Norvegicum (volumes I-XXI)]
2 CONT
2 CONT Dato: 18 Mai 1483. Sted: Stockholm.
2 CONT
2 CONT Till mere wisse och betra forwaringe late wij trycke wore jnsigle meth welborne mendz her Gøtstaff Karlssons och her '''Gregers Matssons''' jnsigle vpo ryggen aa thetta breff Giffuet j Stocholm vpo pynsdaghe dagh Aarum epter gudz 
2 CONC byrd Mcdlxxx tertio 
2 CONT
