1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Væpner Tore Byting, till Stola=
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * Thore Byting was born in ca. 1390 Stola. He died in Stola pa Kallandsay i Veneren, dod etter 1448.. 
2 CONT * Tore Byting was a Swedish squire who is mentioned in contemporary sources between 1416 and 1437–1439. He is believed to have been lord of the manor of Stola in Västergötland , which was held by his widow Holmfrid Jonsdotter in 1
2 CONC 478. It is disputed which coat of arms Tore Byting carried, but it has been assumed to represent an inverted mussel shell. However, a surviving 16th-century drawing of his seal shows a difficult-to-interpret motif that has been de
2 CONC scribed as "three objects, similar to hockey sticks, set in a pole-wise manner" ( Beerståhl ). Byting is above all known as the ancestor of a number of Swedish nobility . A first compilation of his descendants was made in 1579 and
2 CONC  is kept in the National Archives . It has since been published in printed form in 1885 (in the Swedish Autografsällskapets journal ) and 1958 (in Släkt och Hävd ).
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT He married '''Holmfrid Jonsdatter.''' Thore was born in Bodde 1416 i Sverige. Holmfrid Jonsdatter [Parents] died in Stola pa Kallandsay i Veneren. She married Thore Byting.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =They had the following children:=
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Ingrid Thoresdatter Bytting.''' Married Oluf Trulsson Håberg 
2 CONT * '''Ingegjerd Thoresdatter Bytting.'''
2 CONT * '''Ingeborg Thoresdatter Byting was born in 1425.''' Married  Sven Johansson Halv Lilja.
2 CONT * '''Karin Thoresdatter Byting.''' Married  Klaus Christensson Ribbing (Halvmåne) 
2 CONT * '''Byting Olofsson Byting,'''
2 CONT * '''Kerstin Byting.'''
2 CONT * '''Hebla Bytting.'''
2 CONT * '''Anna Bytting.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
