2 CONT Per Joensson, knighted Gyllensvärd, to Önnarp, and Hössna, both in Hössna parish, Älvsborg county. From Sunnerbo district in Småland. Accepted military service in 1607, was an ensign at the Västbo regiment 1618-03-26 and in 1622 a
2 CONC t the muster in Riga was a lieutenant in his brother-in-law Baltzar von Neuman's company of his brother-in-law Johan Hindersson Routers of the Skälboö regiment Västgöta knektar (Skaraborg's regiment). Captain at Nils Ribbing's Väs
2 CONC tgöta regiment (Älvsborg's) in 1624. Transferred to Västgöta horsemen in 1628. Mustered as horseman at Småland's horsemen 1630-06-17 in Kalmar. Knighted 1632-08-12 in the field camp at Nuremberg, but the letter of nobility first s
2 CONC igned 1634-09-10 and confirmed 1647-04-20 (introd. 1638-01-17 under no. 240). Major 1632, at the end of the year. Lieutenant-Colonel in 1633 and subsequently commanded the regiment with a colonel's allowance during the stay of Fre
2 CONC drik Stenbock, wounded at Lützen, at home in the country. Resigned from the regiment in 1641, when he was not appointed its colonel. Commander of a noble banner company at the outbreak of the war with Denmark in 1644 and thus cont
2 CONC ributed significantly to the happy outcome of the battle at Önsvalla pass in Halland. Resigned in 1656. Died 1664-03-19 and buried next year at midsummer in Hössna church. In 1626, he bought Önnarp's tax farm, etc. in Hössna paris
2 CONC h and obtained the right of salvation here on 03/03/1629 at a convenient time. During the following three decades, he formed the manors of Önnarp and Hössna as well as Prästtorp in Berga parish, Kronoberg county, by purchasing the
2 CONC  tax and crown homes in Västergötland and Småland. [ when he was not appointed as its colonel. Commander of a noble banner company at the outbreak of the war with Denmark in 1644 and thus contributed significantly to the happy out
2 CONC come of the battle at Önsvalla pass in Halland. Resigned in 1656. Died 1664-03-19 and buried next year at midsummer in Hössna church. In 1626, he bought Önnarp's tax farm, etc. in Hössna parish and obtained the right of salvation 
2 CONC here on 03/03/1629 at a convenient time. During the following three decades, he formed the manors of Önnarp and Hössna as well as Prästtorp in Berga parish, Kronoberg county, by purchasing the tax and crown homes in Västergötland 
2 CONC and Småland. [ when he was not appointed as its colonel. Commander of a noble banner company at the outbreak of the war with Denmark in 1644 and thus contributed significantly to the happy outcome of the battle at Önsvalla pass in
2 CONC  Halland. Resigned in 1656. Died 1664-03-19 and buried next year at midsummer in Hössna church. In 1626, he bought Önnarp's tax farm, etc. in Hössna parish and obtained the right of salvation here on 03/03/1629 at a convenient tim
2 CONC e. During the following three decades, he formed the manors of Önnarp and Hössna as well as Prästtorp in Berga parish, Kronoberg county, by purchasing the tax and crown homes in Västergötland and Småland. [ at midsummer time in Hö
2 CONC ssna church. In 1626, he bought Önnarp's tax farm, etc. in Hössna parish and obtained the right of salvation here on 03/03/1629 at a convenient time. During the following three decades, he formed the manors of Önnarp and Hössna as
2 CONC  well as Prästtorp in Berga parish, Kronoberg county, by purchasing the tax and crown homes in Västergötland and Småland. [ at midsummer time in Hössna church. In 1626, he bought Önnarp's tax farm, etc. in Hössna parish and obtain
2 CONC ed the right of salvation here on 03/03/1629 at a convenient time. During the following three decades, he formed the manors of Önnarp and Hössna as well as Prästtorp in Berga parish, Kronoberg county, by purchasing the tax and cro
2 CONC wn homes in Västergötland and Småland. [1 ]. '''Married to Elisabet Hand , to Hössna and Gavlö, born 1598, died 1651-04-10 and buried in Hössna church, daughter of the governor Håkan Hand , and Virginia, King Erik XIV's natural da
2 CONC ughter with Agda Persdotter.'''
