1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "Sir John married at the Rolls Chapel, on 7 February 1618-19, <strong>Jane</strong>, daughter of <strong>Richard Sproxtoune of Wakefield</strong>, steward of the Star Chamber, and widow of William Marwood. As widow of Sir John Liv
2 CONC ingston she had a charter of the lands of Dunipace, and married, thirdly, between 1633 and 1645, Edward, first Lord Gorges, and was buried from Lincoln's Inn Fields, at St Margaret's, Westminster, 15 May 1665. In a petition for th
2 CONC e continuance of her pension, dated 1664, she states that she is eighty years old."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun06pauluoft#page/450/mode/2up The Scots peerage], Vol. VI, page 451-452
2 CONT
2 CONT == Notes ==
2 CONT * NAME: In the [http://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun06pauluoft#page/450/mode/2up The Scots peerage] she referenced as <strong>Jane Sproxtoune</strong> and in [http://archive.org/stream/cu31924092524382#page/n341/mode/2up Com
2 CONC plete baronetage] as <strong>Janet Thoxton</strong>
