1 OCCU Adlig, nr 68
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Margareta  Mattiasdotter Kagg=(nr.68)
2 CONT * [https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Kagg_nr_68#TAB_5 Daughter of Mattias Nilsson Kagg and Elin Gustafsdotter ]
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/photo/view/6000000005254417701?album_type=photos_of_me&photo_id=6000000085097593836&position=0 '''Eskilsäter Church, Värmland. Funeral Banner. Family board for Lennart Silfversvärd''']
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married: [https://www.geni.com/photo/view/6000000005254417701?album_type=photos_of_me&photo_id=6000000190555878827 '''Peder Bengtsson Svenske, (nr.258)'''] Sources: EÄ VIII. Sources: EÄ VIII, Tab 4
2 CONT
2 CONT * Peder Svenske (son of Bengt Svenske, Tab. 3), to Rånnum. Shepherd chief in Väne after the father in 1588 and still 1600. Was dead in 1623. Married to Margareta Kagg, daughter of the ruler Mattias Nilsson Kagg (no. 68) and his 2n
2 CONC d wife Elin Gustafsdotter (Forstenaätten).
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children=
2 CONT
2 CONT *'''Lennart. Rittmeister,''' (son of Peder Svenske, Swedish), to Säter in Eskilsäters parish. Ryttmästare. Was dead in 1626. Married to Elin Jakobsdotter, daughter of the unmarried rider Jacob Jonsson to Lång in Grums parish and H
2 CONC olmfrid Pedersdotter (Stårck) (Ramstad's genus)).
2 CONT
2 CONT *'''Captain Johan Svenske,''' son of Peder Svenske Swedish) Married to Märta Thomson, daughter of Colonel Tomas Thomson, natural. Thomson no 299 and Catharina Mauritzdotter Murray.  Children: Hans Månsson Swedish. Born before 1634
2 CONC . Equestrian. Dead 1677
2 CONT
2 CONT *'''Anna Svenskedotter,'''  lived 1640 on the pile in Väne hundred. married before 1618 with Lieutenant Colonel Jens Peders son (Dahlepil, No. 663).
2 CONT
2 CONT *'''Barbro Svenskedotter,''' Married before 1618 with the commanding man in cheeks and marks hundreds Bengt Arvidsson, Gentiles.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Noble Family Forstena Genera=
2 CONT
2 CONT Medieval frälsesläkt from Västergötland. Elders knew the ancestor is Sven Brynjulfsson (1450) to Todene (now great Berg) in Tådene Parish, which in the gun brought a bagghuvud but whose children adopted mödernevapnet (Sparre over 
2 CONC the leaf). 
2 CONT
2 CONT His grandson, Torsten lennarts Son (1561-1631) to Forstena in Tunhems Parish, was introduced on behalf of Oxenstierna 1625 (10/3-4/4) in the second class, the Class of knights, by drawing lots under the No. 5 present No. 2, and ob
2 CONC tained the family name after the farm. 
2 CONT
2 CONT His son Privy Council and Field Marshal Lennart Torstensson (1603-1651), was elevated in both baronial and Grevlig dignity 1647 5/2 at the Royal Palace of Queen Kristina, and was introduced in the same year 15/3 under No. 7 among 
2 CONC counts, but Sword side 1727 20/12. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Another branch of the dynasty was introduced in particular 1625 (10/3-4/4) in the third class, the Svenneklassen, by the draw under the current no 153 with the name Ulffana (after the helmet ornament) and with the same weapons as 
2 CONC the Forstena family, but soon went on the sword side about 1633. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The family descends on mödernet from the so-called Abjörnsönernas, and is thus befryndad with the extinct noble family of RAM AF Berga no 118. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The family was previously extinct since the 1660 century. However, a 1990 in the National Archives found a letter from 1666 1/3 (E 3551, Ekebladssaml., 1: B), that Governor in Värmland and assessor in the Svea Court of Appeal Olof
2 CONC  Christoffer's son (1563-1647) had a hitherto unknown, displaced son. He was the captain of the Närke and the Värmland Regiment Jon Olofsson Dahlman (killed outside Bremen 1675). He became the ancestor of the now living Ättekulla 
2 CONC branch. 
2 CONT
2 CONT By order of the House of nobility 1992 15/12 was granted the introduction of the current Ättekulla branch of the Knights ' house pedigrees under the grandfather name of the Forstena family. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ättekulla members write themselves Dahlman, Wadekar and Järrel.
2 CONT
